esents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\nDuring Q1'2026, average property prices for Sahakar Avenue moved from ₹ 23,600/sqft to ₹ 30,000/sqft, reflecting a 27.12% rise.\n\nExternal Works has reached 100%, Internal finishing stands at 100%, MEP Services including lift and staircases, are now 100% done.\n\nInternal finishing stands at 94%, MEP Services including lift and staircases, are now 95% done.\n\nA total of 34 out of 80 launched units have been booked as of December 2025.\n\nExternal Works has reached 95%, Internal finishing stands at 88%, MEP Services including lift and staircases, are now 86% done.\n\nA total of 34 out of 80 launched units have been booked as of February 2025.\n\n### Govt. Registrations\n\n6 Sales Transactions Registered in Sahakar Avenue From Oct 25 to Sep 26 at Avg. Price ₹ 1